# Removing a project session's orb, and what it may delete: the web
# confirm (GET /api/sessions/{id}/orb/remove, then DELETE on the same
# path), `bough project rm` and `bough project prune`. One session, one
# repo, one worktree ~/.bough/orbs/<session>/<repo> on branch
# bough/<session>. Recipe: go/tests/model/README.md.
#
# orb_lifecycle.fizz models Remove with one dirty flag and one owner.
# This spec is about the gaps between what a plan checks and what Remove
# deletes:
#   - PlanRemove (internal/orb/cleanup.go) computes Dirty from
#     state.json's Worktrees only, while Remove (internal/orb/orb.go)
#     force-removes every dir entry with a .git file and then RemoveAll's
#     the orb dir. Prepare rewrites state.json with no Worktrees at its
#     first write (starting/sync), keeps it empty if the sync fails, and
#     prepareMounts refills it with the project's CURRENT repos only.
#   - the CLI's plan is made, printed and confirmed with [y/N];
#     RemovePlanned then trusts it (its own Dirty check reads the plan).
#   - serve's ownerAlive trusts a pid it did not spawn only if state.json
#     was written after this serve started.
#
# Where the code disagreed with the mapped model (and the code won):
#   - The worktree list is emptied not only when a Prepare fails at
#     sync: EVERY Prepare writes starting(sync) with no Worktrees, so the
#     whole sync (a network fetch, seconds to minutes) is a window, and
#     an owner that dies in it leaves it that way (Resume, OwnerGone).
#   - A serve restart does not leave serve's own children running:
#     Supervisor.Close kills them. Only another bough (cli) survives it,
#     and it reads dead to the new serve until it next writes state.json
#     (ServeRestart, CliWrites).
#   - The page never sends ?branches=1 (api.removeOrb): only another
#     client of the API deletes branches through the web path. The spec
#     takes the worst case, branches pruned on every path; the web
#     re-plans at delete time, so its branch decisions are fresh.
#   - The CLI's owner check is a bare kill(pid, 0): any owner, serve's
#     or another bough's, fresh or not, refuses at plan time.
#   - "Removing", "BranchesDeleted" and "PartialFailure" are not states a
#     client can hold: each remove is one request (or one process) that
#     runs worktree removal, RemoveAll and `git branch -D` in order.
#     They are folded into the removing step; RuntimeRemoveFails is the
#     variant of each step in which the container remove fails.
#   - Branches are deleted even when Remove itself failed (RemovePlanned
#     joins the errors and carries on).
#   - Archived sessions (prune's other reason) are left out: prune
#     eligibility is modelled as the status reason only.
#   - A new orb after a remove has no container and no branch until its
#     start: prepareMounts makes the branch at the base (only for a repo
#     in project.yml) and the start makes the container. A runtime remove
#     can only fail on a container that is there: every runtime's Remove
#     answers nil for a missing one (found by the server walk,
#     mbt/orb_remove_data_safety_test.go; the first spec had both at
#     Prepare, and a failed remove left an orphan with no container).
#
# Fields (role Orb):
#   orb        present | none (dir and container gone) | orphan (dir gone,
#              container left: no state.json names it any more)
#   file       state.json status: sync (starting, before the worktrees
#              are added) | running | failed | stopped | none
#   tracked    state.json's Worktrees names the worktree
#   dirty      the worktree has uncommitted changes
#   branch     bough/<session>: merged (an ancestor of the base, or
#              pushed) | unmerged | deleted
#   inYml      the repo is still in project.yml
#   ctr        the container exists (made by a start, kept by stops)
#   owner      none | serve (serve's child) | cli (another bough that
#              wrote since serve started) | clistale (another bough, alive,
#              whose last write is older than serve)
#   flow       idle | web (the page's confirm is open) | cli (the CLI's
#              [y/N] prompt is waiting)
#   pdirty     the CLI plan's Dirty is non-empty (only while flow == cli)
#   pdel       the CLI plan marks the branch for deletion (idem)
#   Ghosts, set only by a remove, which say HOW it went wrong:
#   lost       a dirty worktree was deleted: "" | untracked (state.json
#              did not name it) | stale (a CLI plan older than the edit)
#              | fresh (a fresh plan named it dirty: must never happen)
#   orphaned   a live owner's orb was deleted: "" | restart (serve read a
#              live CLI as dead) | stale (the CLI plan's owner check was
#              older than the resume) | fresh (must never happen)
#   blost      an unmerged branch was deleted: "" | stale | fresh
#   killed     a refused remove had ended serve's own child first
#   reported   the last remove returned an error (container not removed)

role Orb:
    action Init:
        # A session that ran and exited cleanly: stopped orb, clean
        # worktree on a branch that is still at its base.
        self.orb = "present"
        self.file = "stopped"
        self.tracked = True
        self.dirty = False
        self.branch = "merged"
        self.inYml = True
        self.ctr = True
        self.owner = "none"
        self.flow = "idle"
        self.pdirty = False
        self.pdel = False
        self.lost = ""
        self.orphaned = ""
        self.blost = ""
        self.killed = False
        self.reported = False

    # --- the session ---

    # Prepare's first write: state.json starting(sync) with no Worktrees,
    # PID the new process. serve's child for a web session, another
    # bough for a CLI one. The orb dir (and the worktree in it) stays; a
    # removed orb is made again (MkdirAll; its container, if one was left
    # behind, is found by name).
    atomic action ResumeByServe:
        require self.owner == "none"
        self.owner = "serve"
        self.prepare()

    atomic action ResumeByCli:
        require self.owner == "none"
        self.owner = "cli"
        self.prepare()

    # SyncRepos passed; prepareMounts re-adds (or keeps) a worktree per
    # repo in project.yml and names exactly those, making bough/<session>
    # at the base if a remove deleted it. Build and container start are
    # folded in: they write no Worktrees.
    atomic fair action SyncOk:
        require self.owner != "none" and self.file == "sync"
        self.file = "running"
        self.tracked = self.inYml
        if self.inYml and self.branch == "deleted":
            self.branch = "merged"
        self.ctr = True
        self.wrote()

    # SyncRepos failed: o.fail writes failed with the still-empty map.
    atomic action PrepareFailedAtSync:
        require self.owner != "none" and self.file == "sync"
        self.file = "failed"
        self.wrote()

    # The agent edits the mounted worktree; a repo no longer in
    # project.yml is not mounted, so only a tracked worktree is edited.
    atomic action AgentEdits:
        require self.owner != "none" and self.file == "running" and self.tracked and not self.dirty
        self.dirty = True

    atomic action AgentCommits:
        require self.owner != "none" and self.file == "running" and self.tracked and self.dirty
        self.dirty = False
        self.branch = "unmerged"

    atomic action AgentPushes:
        require self.owner != "none" and self.file == "running" and self.branch == "unmerged"
        self.branch = "merged"

    # The session exits (or crashes). A clean exit's Orb.Stop writes
    # stopped; a crash in sync leaves starting behind, which is the
    # state prune treats as dead.
    atomic action OwnerGone:
        require self.owner != "none"
        self.owner = "none"
        if self.file == "running":
            self.file = "stopped"

    # A live CLI session writes state.json again (an exec restarting the
    # container, a portal): the new serve believes its pid again.
    atomic action CliWrites:
        require self.owner == "clistale" and self.orb == "present"
        self.owner = "cli"

    # The person drops the repo from project.yml. Its worktree stays in
    # the orb dir; the next Prepare no longer names it.
    atomic action RepoRemovedFromProjectYml:
        require self.inYml and self.orb == "present"
        self.inYml = False

    # serve restarts: Close kills its children (their orbs stop), and
    # another bough's pid now predates serve.started.
    atomic action ServeRestart:
        require self.owner in ("serve", "cli")
        if self.owner == "serve":
            self.owner = "none"
            if self.file == "running":
                self.file = "stopped"
        else:
            self.owner = "clistale"

    # --- web: Remove orb in the project page ---

    # GET .../orb/remove, shown in the confirm. The page's plan is only
    # shown: DELETE plans again.
    atomic action OpenRemovePlan:
        require self.orb == "present" and self.flow == "idle"
        self.flow = "web"
        self.killed = False
        self.reported = False

    atomic fair action Cancel:
        require self.flow == "web"
        self.flow = "idle"

    atomic action Confirm:
        require self.flow == "web"
        self.web_delete(False)

    atomic action ConfirmRuntimeRemoveFails:
        require self.flow == "web" and self.ctr
        self.web_delete(True)

    # --- CLI: bough project rm <session> --branches / prune --branches ---

    # ownerAlive (pid alive) refuses; otherwise the plan is printed and
    # the [y/N] prompt waits.
    atomic action CliRm:
        require self.orb == "present" and self.flow == "idle" and self.owner == "none"
        self.cli_plan()

    # prune plans only orbs whose status says nobody resumes them.
    atomic action CliPrune:
        require self.orb == "present" and self.flow == "idle" and self.owner == "none"
        require self.file in ("sync", "failed")
        self.cli_plan()

    atomic action CliYes:
        require self.flow == "cli"
        self.cli_delete(False)

    atomic action CliYesRuntimeRemoveFails:
        require self.flow == "cli" and self.ctr
        self.cli_delete(True)

    atomic fair action CliNo:
        require self.flow == "cli"
        self.flow = "idle"
        self.pdirty = False
        self.pdel = False

    # --yes: plan and remove in one go, no window.
    atomic action CliRmYes:
        require self.orb == "present" and self.flow == "idle" and self.owner == "none"
        self.cli_plan()
        self.cli_delete(False)

    # --- helpers (atomic: see orb_lifecycle.fizz) ---

    atomic func prepare():
        if self.orb != "present":
            # A new orb: the last remove's record is checked already
            # (every assertion runs on the state right after it).
            self.orb = "present"
            self.reported = False
            self.lost = ""
            self.orphaned = ""
            self.blost = ""
        self.file = "sync"
        self.tracked = False
        self.killed = False
        self.wrote()

    atomic func wrote():
        if self.owner == "clistale":
            self.owner = "cli"

    atomic func cli_plan():
        self.flow = "cli"
        self.killed = False
        self.reported = False
        self.pdirty = plan_dirty(self)
        self.pdel = plan_del(self)

    # removeOrb: 404 without an orb; serve's own child killed first;
    # another bough refused while ownerAlive; then a fresh plan and its
    # dirty refusal; then RemovePlanned.
    atomic func web_delete(rtfail):
        self.flow = "idle"
        if self.orb != "present":
            return
        if self.owner == "serve":
            self.killed = True
            self.owner = "none"
            if self.file == "running":
                self.file = "stopped"
        elif self.owner == "cli":
            return
        if plan_dirty(self):
            return
        self.killed = False
        self.remove(plan_del(self), rtfail, False)

    # RemovePlanned on the plan made before the prompt.
    atomic func cli_delete(rtfail):
        self.flow = "idle"
        pd = self.pdirty
        pdel = self.pdel
        self.pdirty = False
        self.pdel = False
        if self.orb != "present" or pd:
            return
        self.remove(pdel, rtfail, True)

    # orb.Remove then the planned `git branch -D`: every worktree dir is
    # force-removed, the orb dir RemoveAll'd whether or not the container
    # remove worked; branches are deleted either way.
    atomic func remove(delb, rtfail, stale):
        if self.dirty:
            if not self.tracked:
                self.lost = "untracked"
            elif stale:
                self.lost = "stale"
            else:
                self.lost = "fresh"
        if self.owner != "none":
            if self.owner == "clistale" and not stale:
                self.orphaned = "restart"
            elif stale:
                self.orphaned = "stale"
            else:
                self.orphaned = "fresh"
        if delb:
            if self.branch == "unmerged":
                self.blost = "stale" if stale else "fresh"
            self.branch = "deleted"
        self.orb = "orphan" if rtfail else "none"
        self.ctr = rtfail
        self.reported = rtfail
        self.file = "none"
        self.tracked = False
        self.dirty = False

# PlanRemove: Dirty from the tracked worktree; the branch marked for
# deletion when merged/pushed, its worktree not dirty, and the repo
# reachable from project.yml or state.json.
def plan_dirty(o):
    return o.tracked and o.dirty

def plan_del(o):
    return o.branch == "merged" and (o.inYml or o.tracked) and not (o.tracked and o.dirty)

action Init:
    orb = Orb()

# No remove deletes uncommitted work it was able to see: a worktree a
# fresh plan names is never deleted dirty. The full claim (lost == "")
# fails; see UntrackedWorktreeLost and StaleCliPlan below.
always assertion NoTrackedDirtyWorkLostOnAFreshPlan:
    return orb.lost in ("", "untracked", "stale")

# A remove never deletes the orb of a session whose owner it could see
# alive. The full claim (owner != none -> orb present) fails; see
# ServeRestartForgetsCliOwner and StaleCliPlan below.
always assertion LiveOwnerKeepsOrb:
    return orb.orphaned in ("", "restart", "stale") and (orb.owner == "none" or orb.orb == "present" or orb.orphaned != "")

# An unmerged branch is never deleted on a fresh plan. The full claim
# (blost == "") fails; see StaleCliPlan below.
always assertion UnmergedBranchKeptOnAFreshPlan:
    return orb.blost in ("", "stale")

# A refused remove deletes nothing: the orb and its worktree are there.
# (It may still have ended the session: see KillBeforeDirtyCheck.)
always assertion RefusedRemoveDeletesNothing:
    return not orb.killed or (orb.orb == "present" and orb.owner == "none")

# A container a remove left behind was reported as an error. Nothing
# else names it afterwards: see OrphanContainer.
always assertion LeftoverContainerReported:
    return orb.orb != "orphan" or orb.reported

# The CLI plan exists only while its prompt waits.
always assertion PlanOnlyWhilePrompting:
    return orb.flow == "cli" or not (orb.pdirty or orb.pdel)

# A remove in progress ends: the confirm and the prompt are answered
# (Cancel / CliNo are fair: a person eventually closes them).
always eventually assertion RemoveEnds:
    return orb.flow == "idle"

# A live owner's sync ends (ok or failed): the empty-Worktrees window
# closes while its process lives.
always eventually assertion SyncWindowCloses:
    return orb.file != "sync" or orb.owner == "none"

# The mapped claims the code breaks. Each was added to this spec as an
# assertion and fails; fizz's shortest counterexamples (action names
# from this spec):
#
# UntrackedWorktreeLost: no remove path deletes a worktree with
# uncommitted changes, including dirs state.json does not name.
#   always assertion NoDirtyWorkLost: lost == ""   (lost == "untracked")
#   ResumeByServe, SyncOk, AgentEdits, OwnerGone, ResumeByServe,
#   OwnerGone, CliRmYes: the second start died in its sync, state.json
#   names no worktree, the plan is clean, Remove force-deletes the dirty
#   one. The same through the web: ... AgentEdits, ServeRestart,
#   ResumeByServe, OpenRemovePlan, Confirm (the DELETE kills the child in
#   its sync first); through prune after PrepareFailedAtSync; and after
#   RepoRemovedFromProjectYml with a successful resume.
#
# StaleCliPlan: a confirmed plan is re-validated (dirty, owner, branch)
# at delete time. `bough project rm` without --yes:
#   (lost == "stale")      CliRm, ResumeByServe, SyncOk, AgentEdits, CliYes
#   (orphaned == "stale")  CliRm, ResumeByServe, CliYes: a session
#                          resumed at the prompt loses its orb; its next
#                          exec recreates a container over missing
#                          worktrees.
#   (blost != "")          CliRm, ResumeByServe, SyncOk, AgentEdits,
#                          AgentCommits, CliYes: the plan's "merged into
#                          <base>" deletes the new unmerged commits.
#
# ServeRestartForgetsCliOwner: remove never deletes the orb of a session
# whose owner is alive in any process.
#   (orphaned == "restart")  ResumeByCli, ServeRestart, OpenRemovePlan,
#                            Confirm.
#
# KillBeforeDirtyCheck: a refused remove changes nothing.
#   always assertion RefusalKeepsSession: not killed
#   ResumeByServe, SyncOk, AgentEdits, OpenRemovePlan, Confirm: 409
#   "uncommitted changes", and serve's child was SIGKILLed first.
#
# OrphanContainer: a remove completes or leaves nothing unnamed.
#   always assertion NoOrphanContainer: orb != "orphan"
#   OpenRemovePlan, ConfirmRuntimeRemoveFails: the error is returned, but
#   the orb dir (the only record naming the container) is gone, so no
#   later list, prune or remove can find it.
